<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title><%= title %></title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css">
</head>
<body>
<header class="hero">
    <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">WEB TECHNOLOGIES LABORATORY</p>
        <h1>Experiment 12</h1>
        <h2>Node.js, Express.js & EJS Templating</h2>
        <p>Server-side JavaScript, REST APIs, URL parameters, POST requests and dynamic EJS pages.</p>
    </div>
</header>

<nav>
    <div class="container nav-inner">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <a href="/students">Students</a>
        <a href="/api/students">REST API</a>
    </div>
</nav>

<main class="container">
    <section class="card">
        <h2>Objective</h2>
        <p>
            To understand server-side JavaScript using Node.js, build RESTful APIs
            using Express.js, handle HTTP requests and responses, work with URL
            parameters and POST data, and render dynamic pages using EJS.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
        <h2>Concepts Demonstrated</h2>
        <div class="grid">
            <article><strong>Node.js</strong><span>Server-side JavaScript runtime</span></article>
            <article><strong>Express.js</strong><span>Routing and HTTP request handling</span></article>
            <article><strong>EJS</strong><span>Dynamic HTML templating</span></article>
            <article><strong>REST API</strong><span>GET, POST and DELETE endpoints</span></article>
            <article><strong>URL Params</strong><span>Example: /student/:id</span></article>
            <article><strong>Nodemon</strong><span>Automatic server restart during development</span></article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
        <h2>Quick API Test</h2>
        <p>Open the endpoint below to see JSON generated by Express:</p>
        <a class="button" href="/api/students">GET /api/students</a>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
        <h2>Current Students</h2>
        <ul class="student-list">
            <% students.forEach(student => { %>
                <li>
                    <div>
                        <strong><%= student.name %></strong>
                        <span><%= student.course %></span>
                    </div>
                    <a href="/student/<%= student.id %>">View</a>
                </li>
            <% }); %>
        </ul>
    </section>
</main>

<footer>Experiment 12 • Node.js + Express.js + EJS</footer>
</body>
</html>